-- title:
--   Stalks of a semistable model are reduced modulo mathfrak m_A
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$. Fix index types $\iota_V, \iota_E$, fields $\overline{F}_i$ ($i \in \iota_V$) each equipped with an algebra structure over the residue field of $A$, component charts $C_i$ of $F$ over $\overline{F}_i$ relative to $A$, annuli $\mathrm{An}_e$ ($e \in \iota_E$) in $F$ over $A$, maps $\mathrm{src}, \mathrm{tgt} : \iota_E \to \iota_V$, and for each $e$ places $x_s(e)$ of $\overline{F}_{\mathrm{src}(e)}$ and $x_t(e)$ of $\overline{F}_{\mathrm{tgt}(e)}$ over the residue field of $A$. Let $M$ be a semistable model for these data: its carrier `M.X` is an integral scheme together with a morphism `M.toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ that is proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, a ring isomorphism of $F$ with the function field of `M.X` carrying $A$ to the image of $A$ under the canonical map to the function field, and a bijective classification of the points of `M.X` as the generic point, the points `pt P` attached to places $P$ of $F/L$, the component generic points `gen i` ($i \in \iota_V$), the smooth special points `sm i Q` for non-nodal places $Q$ of $\overline{F}_i$, and the nodes `nd e` ($e \in \iota_E$), with the local rings, images in $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and specialisation relations prescribed by the chart and annulus data (all of this summarised here). Let $x$ be a point of `M.X` whose image under `M.toBase` is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Then the quotient of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{M.X},x}$ by the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ under the composite $A \to \Gamma(\mathrm{M.X}) \to \mathcal O_{\mathrm{M.X},x}$ (the global-sections map of `M.toBase` followed by the germ map at $x$) is reduced.
--
--   This is the stalkwise form of the statement that the special fibre of a semistable model is reduced, read off from the classification of points of the model and the local rings attached to charts, annuli and nodes. It is used in the proof of [`AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.isReduced_pullback_residue_of_level`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.isReduced_pullback_residue_of_level), where reducedness of the fibre over the closed point is needed at every level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_SemistableModel_isReduced_stalk_quotient_maximalIdeal_of_base_eq_closedPoint.lean

